From 65fdd289c43b9dcd738bb55794fcb92f9f0bd4df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 17:04:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Hades][DV] Profile 20 with an IPT-PQ-c2 base layer is
 rebuilt, never shown as it is nor sent natively

Dolby Vision profile 20 is Dolby Vision in MV-HEVC: the 3D films made for
the Vision Pro, and Apple's only Dolby Vision for stereo video. Dolby's
table of bitstream profiles (Online Delivery Kit) gives it a base layer
signal compatibility of 0 or 4, and defines 0 as it defines profile 5:
"None, Dolby Vision proprietary 10 bit", BT.2020, "PQ with reshaping",
the matrix IPT-PQ-C2 of SMPTE ST 2128.

Kodi took such a stream as one whose base layer is a picture by itself:
BaseLayerIsNoPicture(20, 0) was false, so it was not reconstructed, and
its base view went to the display as PQ BT.2020, with green and purple
colours (what users of other players report of these files). On a
Dolby Vision display it was eligible for native output (any profile
is), which no display was seen taking for profile 20.

- BaseLayerIsNoPicture(): profile 20 with compatibility 0, as profile 5.
  It is rebuilt and sent as HDR10, or mapped to SDR, with either setting
  of "Dolby Vision as HDR10 when needed".
- NativeProfile(): profile 20 never goes out natively (the stream is not
  selected, and its pictures say doviNoNative, as for a choice of the
  user; the log says why). With compatibility 4 it plays as the HLG it
  is.
- CpuPicturesEligible(): its base view decoded by the processor goes to
  the bridge, as profile 5 does (one layer, its own RPU).
- IptPQVideo(): bitmap subtitles of a 20.0 video are those of a PQ video;
  the layer description says "a single layer".

Its two views (a 3D picture) never go out in Dolby Vision: no display
takes Dolby Vision in 3D over HDMI, and a stereoscopic video is never
eligible. Not verified with a real profile 20 file: no sample is legally
at hand.
